package api

import (
	"net/http"
)

var _ = declareRoute(routeDecl{
	Method:      http.MethodPost,
	Pattern:     "/api/v1/issues/{key}/results",
	Auth:        authAny,
	Description: "Record one result of one check: {check, role, verdict, commit, surface?, run?, observed?, negative_control?, failed?, skipped?, excluded?, screenshots?}. {key} is the issue the result is recorded on; check names a check block of its Verification document or of one of its ancestors', by block id or, when a block id is not unique in that set, by its canonical reference (409 CHECK_AMBIGUOUS); any other id is 400 UNKNOWN_CHECK. A check CI proves (GET's definition: ci_check set, when before_merge, no run, a negative_control, and no result recorded against it) is 409 CHECK_PROVED_BY_CI for every role, naming the block and the check run, since its result is read from that run. role is at most 32 characters of a-z and -, verdict is pass or fail, commit is 40 lowercase hex, and each count is from 0 to 2147483647 (the largest the store holds) and defaults to 0; a field outside these bounds is 400 RESULT_INPUT, and a pass counting any failed, skipped or excluded case is 400 RESULT_CONTRADICTS. The commit must be held by the repository the check's issue resolves to, or by a repository in which the external links of the check's issue name a GitHub pull request (https://github.com/<owner>/<repo>/pull/<n>) that is open or merged; a commit that each such repository answers it does not hold is 400 RESULT_COMMIT_UNKNOWN, naming the commit and each owner/repo asked. A link names a pull request only where its owner is a login GitHub serves and its name holds only letters, digits, ., - and _ and is not . or ..; any other link spends no read, and no refusal names it. A linked pull request whose repository's name GitHub's naming rule then refuses, such as one of acme/.git, which is empty once .git is trimmed, counts for nothing and spends one of the 10 reads, and the refusal names that repository as one whose links Dispatch set aside, which no grant of the App mends. One record reads at most 10 linked pull requests, and a refusal says how many it left unread past that bound. Where Dispatch cannot read one of those repositories, the one the check's issue resolves to or a linked one (the App is not installed on it or cannot read it, GitHub's 403 that is no rate limit, or a read of it or of a pull request linked in it does not answer: a rate limit, a 5xx, a transport failure), and no repository is shown to hold the commit, the result is stored, taken to be at a commit of the repository the check's issue resolves to. No repository at all stores the result as before. A screenshot names an image document of the recording issue or of the check's issue. The result is appended as result.recorded on the check's issue. A closed issue, recording or the check's, takes a result only for a check whose when is after_merge or default_branch; every other result there is 409 ISSUE_CLOSED. A check reworded by a document version at each of the two attempts this write makes is 409 CHECK_CONTENDED with Retry-After: 1, the second the version that moved it needs to land, and nothing recorded: read the check and retry. The answer is {result, line}, line being the pull-request body line the result implies: its reading keeps only plain words, every rune a visible letter, a digit or one of . , ; : ! ? ' \" - ( ) /, and of those leaves out every one that holds a link (://), a host below or ending in .internal, a Tailscale MagicDNS host (.ts.net), this Dispatch's own host, or an issue key of a project this Dispatch holds, in any case, and judges the 80-rune cut again, so the line carries no link to Dispatch, no private host, no issue key and no markup.",
	Handler:     (*server).recordCheckResult,
	WriteClass:  scopeProject,
	Shape: routeShape{
		Status: http.StatusCreated, Response: checkResultRecorded{}, Request: checkResultInput{},
	},
})
